{"id": "chatcmpl-5394d987b8c7", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{
  "analysis": "No mount, no isoinfo/7z/xorriso, no pycdlib, and no /dev/kvm (TCG software emulation it is). Only python3 is available. The robust path is to extract the kernel and initramfs from the ISO using a small ISO9660 parser I write in Python, then boot with -kernel/-initrd and supply a serial console append line (mirroring Alpine's isolinux config which sets console=ttyS0). I'll also extract the isolinux config to get the exact APPEND parameters. First, I'll write the ISO parser and dump the directory tree.",
  "plan": "1) Write /tmp/readiso.py — a minimal ISO9660 parser that lists all files and can extract by path. 2) Run it (no args) to dump the full tree to /tmp/tree.txt and print the count, plus filter to boot/ and cfg entries. 3) Inspect to find vmlinuz, initramfs, and the syslinux/isolinux config. Then extract them.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /tmp/readiso.py << 'EOF'\nimport sys, struct, os\nSECTOR=2048\nISO='/app/alpine.iso'\ndef parse_dr(data):\n    if len(data)<34: return None\n    length=data[0]\n    if length==0: return None\n    ext=struct.unpack('<I',data[2:6])[0]\n    dlen=struct.unpack('<I',data[10:14])[0]\n    flags=data[25]\n    nl=data[32]\n    name=data[33:33+nl].split(b';')[0].decode('latin1')\n    return {'ext':ext,'dlen':dlen,'is_dir':bool(flags&2),'name':name}\ndef read_dir(f,lba,length):\n    recs=[]; off=0\n    while off<length:\n        f.seek(lba*SECTOR+off)\n        rl=f.read(1)[0]\n        if rl==0:\n            off=(off//SECTOR+1)*SECTOR\n            continue\n        f.seek(lba*SECTOR+off)\n        rec=f.read(rl)\n        dr=parse_dr(rec)\n        if dr: recs.append(dr)\n        off+=rl\n    return recs\ndef main():\n    f=open(ISO,'rb')\n    f.seek(16*SECTOR)\n    pvd=f.read(SECTOR)\n    root=parse_dr(pvd[156:156+34])\n    results=[]\n    def walk(entries,path):\n        for dr in entries:\n            if dr['name'] in ('.','..'): continue\n            full=(path+'/'+dr['name']) if path else dr['name']\n            results.append((full,dr))\n            if dr['is_dir']:\n                walk(read_dir(f,dr['ext'],dr['dlen']),full)\n    walk(read_dir(f,root['ext'],root['dlen']),'')\n    with open('/tmp/tree.txt','w') as o:\n        for full,_ in results:\n            o.write(full+'\\n')\n    print('total',len(results))\n    for arg in sys.argv[1:]:\n        for full,dr in results:\n            if full.lower()==arg.lower():\n                f.seek(dr['ext']*SECTOR)\n                data=f.read(dr['dlen'])\n                os.makedirs('/app/extracted',exist_ok=True)\n                out='/app/extracted/'+full.replace('/','_')\n                with open(out,'wb') as o:\n                    o.write(data)\n                print('extracted',full,'->',out,dr['dlen'])\n                break\n        else:\n            print('NOT FOUND',arg)\n    f.close()\nmain()\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
